/design and /floor-studio are not duplicates: the studio shows a floor to
somebody who does not yet know what they want, and the configurator is where
somebody who does finishes the specification. They share one catalogue, one
pricing function and one handoff. That was true in the source and invisible
everywhere else.

Floor Studio led the primary navigation alone. /design was reachable only from
the footer, had no breadcrumb schema, no markdown twin, and the only absolute
canonical in the app. A person using the header found one door; a retrieval
system asking whether this site lets you specify a floor found the same one.

  · /design joins Floor Studio in the header, with notes that say which is which
  · /design.md — the configurator's machine edition, naming both doors and what
    each is for, listed in /md alongside the studio's
  · /design gets the breadcrumb schema it never had and a relative canonical
  · both pages state the pairing in prose

Also fixes a live 404: /floor-studio.md was declared in MARKDOWN_TWINS and in
the page's own alternates.types when the studio shipped, but no rewrite was ever
added — so the Link header and <head> advertised a twin that did not resolve.
verify-markdown only checks the rewrites it can see, so nothing caught it. It
now reports 20 surfaces, up from 18.

